2) Architecture & flow (high level)

1. User clicks “Download”. Frontend calls our backend to create / initialize a payment request (amount 20 LD, recipient wallet = +231770251042, metadata: mediaId, buyerId).


2. Backend calls Orange’s API to request payment or create a hosted payment / push request (depends on Orange API for Liberia). Backend stores a pending transaction in Firestore/DB and returns a paymentRequestId or a redirect URL / payment instructions to frontend. 


3. Customer pays from their Orange Money app to the merchant/wallet (or follows hosted page / accepts push). Orange then calls our webhook (configured in Orange merchant portal) with the transaction status.


4. Webhook verifies the signature (if Orange supplies one) or confirms transaction with Orange’s status API, marks the transaction confirmed in DB, and returns success.


5. Frontend polls or receives push (via WebSocket/Server-Sent Events) and unlocks the download when DB shows confirmed. Admin dashboard logs the sale.




