5) Frontend: how to initiate a payment and unlock download

1. Frontend calls /api/payments/initiate with { mediaId, buyerPhone }.


2. Backend returns txId and either a redirect URL or instructions. Display those to the buyer.


3. After payment, frontend polls Firestore (or backend API /api/payments/status?txId=...) until status: confirmed.


4. When confirmed, frontend requests /api/download?mediaId=...&txId=... which validates downloads doc and returns a signed URL (Cloud Storage signed URL) or serves the file.



Frontend pseudo:

// call backend
const r = await fetch('/api/payments/initiate', { method:'POST', body: JSON.stringify({mediaId, buyerPhone})});
const j = await r.json();
// show instructions: "Send 20 LD to +231770251042" OR follow redirect if provided.
// Poll status:
const poll = setInterval(async ()=>{
  const s = await fetch(`/api/payments/status?txId=${j.txId}`).then(r=>r.json());
  if(s.status==='confirmed'){ clearInterval(poll); unlockDownload(s.downloadToken); }
}, 3000);


